# display_gap_suspend_restore_variants: Displays that restore without re-presenting: port 0 connected and acked, never presented, comes back on a display with no mode list, so the machine runs on the restored page's modes alone (no change, nothing raised); port 1 with an ack pending stays pending ("bogus ack"); port 2 with a glyph and show re-sends both to the new display; port 3's display had no modes, so its page restores with a mode count of 0 and connects from the new display's list (4); port 4, acked, whose guest zeroed the mode count, is not "restored" (the page has no modes) but takes the new display's list as an update (12, expectedAck 2, state 1), not a disconnect; port 5 presented and then went to sleep, so the restore only puts it to sleep again (no frame, no call).
